e " data-role=3D"message" dir=3D"auto"><div><p>The shaders are the same as =
from the previous tutorial, but with different uniforms in the vertex shade=
r, and with gl_Position being calculated using them to transform the vertex=
 position between coordinate systems. I'll paste both shaders below.</p><p>=
Vertex shader:</p><p>#version 330 core</p><p>layout (location =3D 0) in vec=
3 aPos;<br>layout (location =3D 1) in vec2 aTexCoord;</p><p>out vec2 TexCoo=
rd;</p><p>uniform mat4 model;<br>uniform mat4 view;<br>uniform mat4 project=
ion;</p><p>void main()<br>{<br>    gl_Position =3D projection * view * mode=
l * vec4(aPos, 1.0);<br>    TexCoord =3D vec2(aTexCoord.x, 1.0 - aTexCoord.=
y);<br>}</p><p>Fragment shader:</p><p>#version 330 core</p><p>out vec4 Frag=
Color;</p><p>in vec2 TexCoord;</p><p>uniform sampler2D texture1;<br>uniform=
 sampler2D texture2;</p><p>void main()<br>{<br>    FragColor =3D mix(textur=
e(texture1, TexCoord), texture(texture2, TexCoord), 0.2);<br>}</p></div></d=
